        "type": "Module",
        "name": "preamp_audio",
        "description": "NE5532 dual low-noise op-amp configured as single-channel non-inverting preamplifier. Channel 1: non-inverting input (IN1_P) receives bias/control voltage from MCP4725 through input network, inverting input (IN1_N) receives feedback network, output (OUT1) is the amplified audio signal. Channel 2: unused, with IN2_P and IN2_N tied to safe bias state (mid-rail or ground-referenced bias to prevent noise pickup), OUT2 left unconnected. Powered from VIN_5V (analog supply) with VCC_P to positive rail and VCC_N to ground. Separate analog ground return strategy: star point or ferrite bead isolation from digital GND at power entry point recommended for low noise.",
